From: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvethernet: Fix NULL pointer in of_get_mac_address call

The ether_get_mac_address() function declared a NULL pointer 'addr' and
passed it to of_get_mac_address(), which attempts to write the MAC
address to that location. This causes undefined behavior - either memory
corruption or failure to retrieve the MAC address.

The fix uses the already-declared mac_addr[ETH_ALEN] buffer instead,
which was the apparent original intent.

This fixes ethernet initialization failures ("jam") on Orin AGX when
running as a VM guest under seL4.

Upstream-Status: Pending [NVIDIA L4T bug]

Signed-off-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/nvidia/nvethernet/ether_linux.c | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/nvidia/nvethernet/ether_linux.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/nvidia/nvethernet/ether_linux.c
index 4f354b0a..c25a526a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/nvidia/nvethernet/ether_linux.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/nvidia/nvethernet/ether_linux.c
@@ -4741,7 +4741,6 @@ static int ether_get_mac_address(struct ether_priv_data *pdata)
 	struct net_device *ndev = pdata->ndev;
 	struct device_node *np = dev->of_node;
 	const char *eth_mac_addr = NULL;
-	u8 *addr = NULL;
 	unsigned char mac_addr[ETH_ALEN] = {0};
 	/* Default choesn node property name for MAC address */
 	char str_mac_address[ETH_MAC_STR_LEN] = "nvidia,ether-mac";
@@ -4788,12 +4787,12 @@ static int ether_get_mac_address(struct ether_priv_data *pdata)
 		 * upstream driver should have only this call to get
 		 * MAC address
 		 */
-		ret = of_get_mac_address(np, addr);
+		ret = of_get_mac_address(np, mac_addr);
 		if (ret < 0) {
 			dev_err(dev, "No Mac address local DT!\n");
 			return ret;
 		}
-		eth_mac_addr = addr;
+		eth_mac_addr = mac_addr;
 	}

 	/* Found a valid mac address */
--
